---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Solar Sunlight Hours in Thailand: Monthly Peak Sun Guide';
const description = 'Thailand averages 4.5-6.5 peak sun hours daily. Explore monthly and regional sunlight data to estimate your solar system output and savings.';
const keywords = 'sunlight hours Thailand, peak sun hours Thailand, solar potential Thailand, solar irradiance Thailand, best months for solar Thailand';
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": title,
    "description": description,
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "datePublished": "2024-06-01",
    "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://www.kohchangsolarcell.com/guides/solar-sunlight-hours/" }
  }}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Guides</span> / <span>Sunlight Hours</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Solar Sunlight Hours in Thailand: Your Monthly Peak Sun Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">
      Understanding sunlight patterns is the first step to estimating your solar system's performance. 
      Thailand's tropical climate delivers excellent solar potential year-round.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-solar-green/5 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-solar-green">5.5</div>
        <div>
          <div class="font-semibold">Average Peak Sun Hours</div>
          <div class="text-gray-600 text-sm">per day, nationwide average</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why Thailand Is Ideal for Solar Energy</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Thailand sits between 5°N and 20°N latitude, placing it in one of the world's best solar zones. 
        The country receives abundant sunshine throughout the year, with only minor variations during the monsoon season.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>High irradiance:</strong> 4.5–6.5 kWh/m²/day across most regions</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Consistent sunshine:</strong> Even rainy months average 3–4 peak hours</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Hot climate advantage:</strong> Higher temperatures slightly reduce efficiency, but longer days compensate</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Monthly Peak Sun Hours by Region</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <th class="p-3 text-left border">Month</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Bangkok (Central)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Chiang Mai (North)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Udon Thani (NE)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Phuket (South)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Trat (East)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Jan</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.2</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.1</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Feb</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.4</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Mar</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.1</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.4</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.2</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Apr</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.1</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.9</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">May</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.2</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.1</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Jun</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.6</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.9</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.7</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Jul</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.6</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.2</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.4</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Aug</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.6</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.4</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.7</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.5</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Sep</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.1</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">4.9</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Oct</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.5</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.3</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.6</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.2</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.4</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Nov</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.1</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.8</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.9</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border font-medium">Dec</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.1</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">5.9</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.2</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.0</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">6.0</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">Values represent average daily peak sun hours (kWh/m²/day). Data sourced from NASA satellite measurements.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">What Does This Mean for Your Solar System?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Peak sun hours tell you how much energy your panels can generate. A 5 kW system in Bangkok produces roughly:
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-solar-green">25–32 kWh</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Daily (average)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-solar-green">750–960 kWh</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Monthly</div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-solar-green">9,000–11,500 kWh</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Yearly</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Best Months for Solar Installation</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        While solar works year-round, <strong>November to February</strong> offer the highest output in most regions. 
        Installing during the rainy season (May–October) means your system is ready to capture maximum energy when the dry season begins.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Sunlight Hours Affect System Sizing</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        A home in Phuket (6.5 peak hours) needs fewer panels than the same home in Chiang Mai (6.0 hours) to produce the same energy. 
        When sizing your system, installers calculate using your <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing-calculator/" class="text-solar-green underline">monthly electricity bill</a> 
        and local peak sun data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/guides/solar-panels-cloudy-days/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Do Solar Panels Work on Cloudy Days?</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Monsoon performance in Thailand</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing-calculator/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Solar System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Size your system by electricity bill</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-panel-maintenance/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Maintenance & Cleaning Guide</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Keep your panels performing at peak</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Ready to Harness Thailand's Sunshine?</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Calculate your system's potential with a free on-site assessment.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Calculate Your System's Potential — Get a Free Quote
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 opacity-80">
        We serve all regions of Thailand from our base in <a href="/" class="underline">Koh Chang</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
